15
00:00:38,294 --> 00:00:41,186
company it's about, scores the sentiment from

16
00:00:41,186 --> 00:00:43,667
minus one to plus one, classifies the

17
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:46,165
type of event, and predicts its market

18
00:00:46,165 --> 00:00:47,757
impact on a scale of one to

19
00:00:47,757 --> 00:00:50,661
ten. Every score comes with the words

20
00:00:50,661 --> 00:00:53,065
that produced it, so an analyst can

21
00:00:53,065 --> 00:00:54,001
see exactly why.

22
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:57,529
Those signals are published to a file,

23
00:00:57,490 --> 00:00:59,387
a REST API, and a live stream.

24
00:00:59,387 --> 00:01:02,387
Two modules subscribe to that stream. A

25
00:01:02,387 --> 00:01:06,027
tactical index rebalancer, and a strategic stress

26
00:01:06,027 --> 00:01:08,532
tester for a wholesale banking book. Let's

27
00:01:08,532 --> 00:01:10,225
